nio: put the root-device name and mount result on the panel

The photograph of run 591 shows bsd_init reaching setconf and then
stopping with no panic, no wait message and no further phase.
The next step in the source is vfs_mountroot(), inside a loop that
retries for ever when mounting fails; its only report goes through
printf, which is frozen by this point, so a failed mount is silent.

Put direct-to-framebuffer marks around that call: the root device
name before the mount, and OK or FAIL after it.  These use nio_bmark,
the same unbuffered writer that produces the phase lines on the
panel, so the next photograph will say exactly which root device was
tried and whether the mount succeeded.  No behaviour changes.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
index 86ce659..37b0174 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -1048,7 +1048,11 @@ bsd_init(void)
 
 		bsd_init_kprintf("vfs_mountroot\n");
 		boot_progress_stage("vfs_mountroot enter");
+		nio_bmark("\nnio: ROOT pre-mount rootdev=[");
+		nio_bmark(rootdevice);
+		nio_bmark("]");
 		if (0 == (err = vfs_mountroot())) {
+			nio_bmark("\nnio: ROOT mount OK");
 			boot_progress_stage("vfs_mountroot mounted; authentication pending");
 			break;
 		}
@@ -1066,6 +1070,7 @@ bsd_init(void)
 			/*NOTREACHED*/
 		}
 #endif
+		nio_bmark("\nnio: ROOT mount FAIL retry");
 		printf("cannot mount root, errno = %d\n", err);
 	}
 
